# Copy to `.env` and edit. Nothing here is secret, and only the six server
# variables at the end may ever hold one: every NEXT_PUBLIC_ value is inlined
# into the JavaScript the browser downloads, so a key must never be one.
#
# The app runs with this file's defaults and no backend at all. Sign in with
# phone 0914378064, code 111002.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Which implementation answers `api.*`
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# `mock` (the default) fakes every group in the browser; `live` makes real HTTP
# requests to NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_MODE=mock

# Groups forced live while the rest stay mocked, comma separated. The accepted
# names are `API_GROUPS` in src/api/contracts.ts — `auth` and `leads` today;
# the remaining groups of docs/api-contract.md (tenant, assistant,
# receptionist) are declared there as the screens that call them arrive.
#
# This exists because Fonnus-BE ships endpoints one at a time over weeks. With
# only a global switch, the first real endpoint could not be exercised until
# every other one existed — which is the difference between integrating
# incrementally and integrating in one terrifying step.
#
# `leads` is the one group Fonnus-BE does not serve: live, the three marketing
# forms post to this app's own /api/leads, /api/leads/hotline-report and
# /api/leads/waitlist, never to NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL, and those route
# handlers need the three Google variables near the end of this file
# (docs/adr/0005).
#
# The landing page's voice demo (`api.voice`) is not a group you can switch:
# it has no mock and always talks to the ElevenLabs agent, with a ticket from
# this app's own /api/voice-demo/token, never NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL. Without
# the three voice demo variables at the end of this file the call screen says it
# could not connect (docs/adr/0006, docs/adr/0007, docs/adr/0009).
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_LIVE_GROUPS=

# Where live requests go. Relative by default so the browser talks to this
# origin and the cookie stays first-party; see docs/adr/0003 for the production
# posture and docs/api-contract.md §1 for why it matters.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=/api/v1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Development proxy
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# In `next dev`, requests to /api/v1/* are rewritten to this origin
# (next.config.ts). Unset means no rewrite — every live call then 404s against
# this app itself, which is the honest failure when the backend is not running.
API_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:4000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shaping the mocks
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# How long the mock pretends the network takes, in milliseconds. Set to 0 for a
# snappy demo.
NEXT_PUBLIC_MOCK_LATENCY_MS=450

# Fraction of mock requests that fail, 0..1. Not decoration: the loading,
# rollback and retry paths cannot be reached in mock mode any other way, so this
# is the only way to look at them before a backend exists. Set it to 1 and walk
# the app.
NEXT_PUBLIC_MOCK_FAILURE_RATE=0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The leads spreadsheet (docs/adr/0005-leads-to-google-sheets.md)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Secrets, so never prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ and never committed with a value. Read
# only by the route handlers, through src/server/env.ts, at request time. Left
# empty, every POST /api/leads… route answers 503 and stores nothing.

# The Google Cloud service account that appends the rows, and the private key
# from its JSON key file. The key may be pasted as one line with literal \n
# where the line breaks were.
GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_EMAIL=
GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PRIVATE_KEY=

# The id in the spreadsheet's URL: docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/<id>/edit.
# Its `leads` tab receives the contact form, `hotline_report` the report
# requests, `waitlist` the waitlist sign-ups (README.md lists the columns).
LEADS_SPREADSHEET_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The landing voice demo (docs/adr/0006-elevenlabs-landing-voice-demo.md)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Secrets, so never prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ and never committed with a value. Read
# only by the route handlers, through src/server/env.ts, at request time. With
# any of the three empty, POST /api/voice-demo/token and GET
# /api/voice-demo/budget answer 503 and the call screen says it could not
# connect to Linh. That is the kill switch: unset the key and the demo stops.
# It is also how to hear the agent locally: put all three in `.env.local`.

# An API key from the ElevenLabs dashboard. Restrict it to the Conversational AI
# scope if the dashboard offers scopes.
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# The agent's id. The browser never sees it.
ELEVENLABS_AGENT_ID=

# A long random string that signs the visitor's budget cookie, the three
# minutes an hour (docs/adr/0009). Make one with `openssl rand -hex 32`, and a
# different one per environment. Rotating it gives every visitor a fresh hour,
# once.
VOICE_DEMO_COOKIE_SECRET=
